    },
    "body": "The type registry is meant to list every PSBT field so new BIPs don't pick a key type that is already taken, but the per-input table skips 0x19. That value is `PSBT_IN_P2C_TWEAK` from BIP-372 (Pay-to-contract tweak fields for PSBT). It was never in the per-input table of BIP-174 either, so the row got lost when the tables moved into the registry.\n\nThis adds the row between `PSBT_IN_TAP_MERKLE_ROOT` (0x18) and `PSBT_IN_MUSIG2_PARTICIPANT_PUBKEYS` (0x1a). I also checked every `PSBT_* = 0x..` definition across the BIPs against the registry, and this was the only one missing.\n",
